{"id": "EUVD-2026-38824", "enisaUuid": "13278d9c-a900-359f-b5a4-597737fe1fbd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlibceph: Fix potential out-of-bounds access in __ceph_x_decrypt()\n\nIn __ceph_x_decrypt(), a part of the buffer p is interpreted as a\nceph_x_encrypt_header, and the magic field of this struct is accessed.\nThis happens without any guarantee that the buffer is large enough to\nhold this struct. The function parameter ciphertext_len represents the\nlength of the ciphertext to decrypt and is guaranteed to be at most the\nremaining size of the allocated buffer p. However, this value is not\nnecessarily greater than sizeof(ceph_x_encrypt_header). E.g., a message\nframe of type FRAME_TAG_AUTH_REPLY_MORE, that is just as long to hold\nthe ciphertext at its end with a ciphertext_len of 8 or less, can\ntrigger an out-of-bounds memory access when accessing hdr->magic.\n\nThis patch fixes the issue by adding a check to ensure that the\ndecrypted plaintext in the buffer is large enough to represent at least\nthe ceph_x_encrypt_header.", "datePublished": "2026-06-24T16:28:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:41:40", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/759053333a40c6997c2917dcd6160bfe40d2b42e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ebc7eddf6225b87e3aae720875f9dd40cb6b1cef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5df268406ef38d0f92547959296577c7077dacdc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c7e9b53aebe401970f1b5f5a01b4e021b18e8bb2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/821365487aa58d06bda65c676ba215d506ba9768"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-52956", "GHSA-wvxf-4p9h-5vg9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.63, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3545979c-ef31-3147-8447-bb44d03c30a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e15fd0a11db00fc7f470a9fc804657ec3f6d04a5 <5df268406ef38d0f92547959296577c7077dacdc"}, {"id": "43bcdfa8-19c2-3437-8ad8-508115c6da00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.10"}, {"id": "550d96a8-43b2-3baa-b4b3-1abe3f5a4028", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e15fd0a11db00fc7f470a9fc804657ec3f6d04a5 <759053333a40c6997c2917dcd6160bfe40d2b42e"}, {"id": "661a3205-b106-3004-b784-e5e7d8ecd195", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.10"}, {"id": "84bfa9c1-abc6-3040-bbe1-e48819dfd405", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "92ef511f-5035-34c6-a431-eeb916f1a83a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e15fd0a11db00fc7f470a9fc804657ec3f6d04a5 <821365487aa58d06bda65c676ba215d506ba9768"}, {"id": "98794945-00ff-35d6-9aea-3c165a23211c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e15fd0a11db00fc7f470a9fc804657ec3f6d04a5 <ebc7eddf6225b87e3aae720875f9dd40cb6b1cef"}, {"id": "9949692d-3331-3537-85f2-b5d98f4661af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "b33a9928-4b1b-3c54-b794-b903b64a6dd0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e15fd0a11db00fc7f470a9fc804657ec3f6d04a5 <c7e9b53aebe401970f1b5f5a01b4e021b18e8bb2"}, {"id": "cbf04c57-10ce-377b-b3e3-add2334d633d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d5c2cb83-9a3a-368f-a48d-c066118765a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9.6 <4.10"}, {"id": "d656151b-3366-317b-9a32-9aebc88d57e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e9fa0739-9bb2-3d54-b0e7-59bcbff76d5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2982b9c92a66604ffb9fb2db